Evergreen-Patch: package-bundled-extensions
Why: Firefox packages the distribution/ directory only in Mozilla's own
  builds (--built-by-mozilla). Evergreen bundles uBlock Origin there
  (`eg.py fetch-extensions`, staged by `eg.py package`); Firefox installs
  extensions from distribution/extensions into each new profile.
Upstream: not upstreamable (Mozilla's packaging choice for its own builds)
Drop-when: Evergreen stops bundling extensions
Owner: Evergreen maintainers

--- a/browser/installer/package-manifest.in
+++ b/browser/installer/package-manifest.in
@@ -461,3 +461,6 @@
 #if defined(BUILT_BY_MOZILLA)
 @RESPATH@/distribution/*
 #endif
+
+; Evergreen: extensions bundled by `eg.py package` (uBlock Origin).
+@RESPATH@/distribution/extensions/*
